          "date": "2026-11-03 16:06:51.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: drop fixed waits in sanity 56oe and 228",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: drop fixed waits in sanity 56oe and 228\n\ntest_56oe sleeps 60 s twice to make three groups of files\nwith different ctimes, then finds the middle group with\nlfs find and 30 s of margin on each side.  The margin only\nhas to cover the time between reading the clock and lfs\nfind reading it; with 2 s it failed (LU-16946).  Sleep 20 s\nwith 10 s margins.\n\ntest_228a, 228b and 228c sleep 6 s after each sync on the\nMDS before reading the OI file's block count with debugfs.\nsync has already committed the journal and written the\ndevice back when it returns.  Remove the sleeps.\n\nTogether about 116 s per run, about 580 hours of test time\nper 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"56oe 228a 228b 228c\",ONLY_REPEAT=10\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I09de32b46b4b4f7774ff989ffe8a9200ff7479b4\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
